{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-tag-tsx","path":"/tag/wildflower/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Joseph Crawford","description":"A blog relating to technical topics such as programming, web development, and software engineering.","siteUrl":"https://josephcrawford.com"}},"tagsJson":{"name":"Wildflower","slug":"wildflower","description":"Wildflower honey, foraged ingredients, and floral fermentations."},"allMarkdownRemark":{"nodes":[{"id":"e1e7cbdd-60c7-54d4-ac6d-8e16ffb4e9ea","html":"<h2>Notes</h2>\n<p>This dandelion mead is ready to drink immediately after bottling — no bottle aging required.</p>\n<p>The fermentation was remarkably straightforward. Red Star Premier Côte is a reliable yeast that ferments cleanly and flocculates well, leaving behind a mead that's bright and easy to drink.</p>\n<p><strong>About the photos:</strong> I don't have many images of this brew because I threw it together quickly once I had the flowers deconstructed. The process was impromptu — once the petals were separated from the stems, everything moved fast.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h2>Tasting Notes</h2>\n<p>The finished mead pours a pale golden color with excellent clarity. The nose carries distinct floral notes — partly from the Ambrosia honey, partly from the dandelion tea. On the palate, it's lightly sweet with a dry finish. The dandelion contributes an herbal, almost tea-like quality that makes this mead feel both rustic and refined. It's refreshing served slightly chilled.</p>","fields":{"readingTime":1},"frontmatter":{"slug":"dandelion-mead","title":"Dandelion Mead","excerpt":"A bright, floral mead made with foraged dandelion flowers and Ambrosia honey. The dandelion tea brings a subtle herbal quality that pairs beautifully with the honey's sweetness.","featuredImage":"/images/content/brewing/dandelion-mead/featured.jpg","tags":["brewing","mead","dandelion","wildflower"],"author":"joseph-crawford","publishedAt":"2026-05-19","rating":null,"draft":null,"review":null,"series":null}}],"totalCount":1},"allTagsJson":{"nodes":[{"slug":"work","name":"Work"},{"slug":"lifestyle","name":"Lifestyle"},{"slug":"food","name":"Food"},{"slug":"family","name":"Family"},{"slug":"sports","name":"Sports"},{"slug":"reviews","name":"Reviews"},{"slug":"ai","name":"AI"},{"slug":"development","name":"Development"},{"slug":"developer-tools","name":"Developer Tools"},{"slug":"mysql","name":"MySQL"},{"slug":"database","name":"Database"},{"slug":"backend","name":"Backend"},{"slug":"engineering","name":"Engineering"},{"slug":"team-culture","name":"Team Culture"},{"slug":"blog","name":"Blog"},{"slug":"opinions","name":"Opinions"},{"slug":"wordpress","name":"WordPress"},{"slug":"security","name":"Security"},{"slug":"supply-chain","name":"Supply Chain"},{"slug":"open-source","name":"Open Source"},{"slug":"typescript","name":"TypeScript"},{"slug":"javascript","name":"JavaScript"},{"slug":"php","name":"PHP"},{"slug":"machine-learning","name":"Machine Learning"},{"slug":"tts","name":"TTS"},{"slug":"voice-ui","name":"Voice UI"},{"slug":"space","name":"Space"},{"slug":"nasa","name":"NASA"},{"slug":"artemis","name":"Artemis"},{"slug":"moon","name":"Moon"},{"slug":"mars","name":"Mars"},{"slug":"hardware","name":"Hardware"},{"slug":"mouse","name":"Mouse"},{"slug":"productivity","name":"Productivity"},{"slug":"accessories","name":"Accessories"},{"slug":"keyboards","name":"Keyboards"},{"slug":"ergonomics","name":"Ergonomics"},{"slug":"programming","name":"Programming"},{"slug":"learning","name":"Learning"},{"slug":"web-development","name":"Web Development"},{"slug":"gaming","name":"Gaming"},{"slug":"smart-home","name":"Smart Home"},{"slug":"basketball","name":"Basketball"},{"slug":"shopping","name":"Shopping"},{"slug":"online","name":"Online"},{"slug":"banking","name":"Banking"},{"slug":"furniture","name":"Furniture"},{"slug":"desks","name":"Desks"},{"slug":"office","name":"Office"},{"slug":"groceries","name":"Groceries"},{"slug":"wedding","name":"Wedding"},